[I] Jakarta Commons Collections

[T] The Java Collections Framework was a major addition in JDK 1.2. It
[T] added many powerful data structures that accelerate development of
[T] most significant Java applications. Since that time it has become the
[T] recognised standard for collection handling in Java.
[T]
[T] Commons-Collections seek to build upon the JDK classes by providing
[T] new interfaces, implementations and utilities.

[U] https://commons.apache.org/proper/commons-collections/

[A] Apache Jakarta Commons team
[M] Minto van der Sluis <minto@multimach.com>

[C] extra/development

[L] OpenSource
[V] 4.6.0

[D] 8ceeb8a6cb06c9f9e4a19675286b78b3a6740c833e7d5aa7b4ba7163 commons-collections4-4.6.0-src.tar.gz https://dlcdn.apache.org//commons/collections/source/

